# Build context is the repo root for both images (docker build -f
# backend/Dockerfile . and -f frontend/Dockerfile ., see docker-compose*.yml).
# Allow list: `*` excludes everything, then one `!` entry per path the two
# Dockerfiles read, so a file dropped anywhere else in the checkout (a key, a
# dump, an agent scratch dir, docs) never reaches the daemon. The entries mirror
# the COPY lines of backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile and the files
# those builds read: npm ci needs the root lockfile and all three workspace
# manifests, the backend build needs tsconfig.json + src + prisma, the frontend
# build needs tsconfig.json, next.config.ts, postcss.config.mjs, eslint.config.mjs,
# src and public. BuildKit matches parent paths too, so a `!dir` entry covers
# everything below that directory and the paired `!dir/**` entries are
# belt-and-braces, not required; a `!` entry only survives what comes after it,
# so the excludes below stay a second layer that prunes inside the allow list
# (nothing here ships a .env at all, so `.env.example` is not excepted: no
# Dockerfile copies it).
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json

!backend/package.json
!backend/tsconfig.json
!backend/prisma
!backend/prisma/**
!backend/src
!backend/src/**

!frontend/package.json
!frontend/tsconfig.json
!frontend/next.config.ts
!frontend/postcss.config.mjs
!frontend/eslint.config.mjs
!frontend/public
!frontend/public/**
!frontend/src
!frontend/src/**

!mcp/package.json

# Second layer: keep secrets and host-built artifacts out even under an entry
# above (they are matched anywhere in the tree, so a key committed inside a
# source directory stays out of the context too). This keeps every exclude of
# the old denylist that can appear inside an allowed directory; the rest are
# covered by the allow list itself: .git, .github, .ai, .claude and docs are
# top-level paths no `!` entry names, and the only tests directories in the
# checkout (backend/tests, frontend/tests, mcp/tests) sit outside the allowed
# directories.
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.npmrc
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
